---
pagination:
  data: collections.themes
  size: 1
  alias: strand
permalink: "/themes/{{ strand.slug }}/index.html"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ strand.title }}"
  seoTitle: "{{ strand.seoTitle }}"
  description: "{{ strand.description }}"
ogImage: "/images/og/tags.png"
layout: layouts/base.njk
---

{% block head %}
{% set crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Themes', url: '/themes/' },
  { name: strand.title, url: page.url }
] %}
{% include "partials/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
{% endblock %}

<div class="posts-header">
  <h1>{{ strand.title }}</h1>
  <p class="post-excerpt">{{ strand.description }}</p>
</div>

<ul class="post-list">
{% for post in strand.posts %}
  <li>
    <div class="post-meta">{{ post.date | postDate }} &middot; {{ authors[post.data.author].name }}</div>
    <h2><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h2>
    {% if post.data.description %}<p class="post-excerpt">{{ post.data.description }}</p>{% endif %}
  </li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<aside class="read-next">
  <p class="section-label">The frame behind all three themes</p>
  <div class="related-item">
    <h3><a href="/posts/010-relationship-design/">Relationship Design</a></h3>
    <p class="post-excerpt">The pillar essay: the interaction is a relationship, it already has terms, and you either chose them or inherited them.</p>
  </div>
</aside>
